  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Carta celeste de Atreia",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Carta celeste de Atreia\"**\n\nCharacters are astros on a star chart. Each one is a glass sphere of liquid light ringed by 56 four-point stars (one per +15 OD, 840 cap), and a gold meridian on a tick ruler measures time to the next recharge. The page is a flat chart: slate ground, 1px rules, square corners, no glass, no card shadows. Luz is a mid-tone golden dusk on slate (nothing white); Sombra is the violet Abyss with silver rules. Both are dark worlds; the same crimson marks \"at cap\" in both.\n\nDensity is calm and ruled: flat rows divided by hairlines rather than boxed cards. Everything that is not the orb is quiet so that the one hot thing (an astro at cap, crimson) reads first.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Two dark faction themes switched by `data-faction` on `<html>`; every colour on the page is a token.",
      "Rules, not boxes: 1px gold (Luz) or silver (Sombra) lines, square corners everywhere.",
      "Marcellus for brand, character names and section headings; Gothic A1 for UI with tabular numerals.",
      "One authored motion moment: the orb recharge ripple and the crimson cap beat.",
      "Authored line icons, drawn orbs; no photography, no 3D, no particles behind the page."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Crimson-Means-Cap Rule",
        "body": "Crimson appears only for an astro at cap (or a destructive/error state). It is never decoration and never a faction accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token-Only Rule",
        "body": "No component writes a colour; it reads a variable, so both factions stay in step. The only literal is the crimson family, shared by both themes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold-Is-The-Accent Rule",
        "body": "`--gold` is whichever accent the faction owns; do not hard-code gold into Sombra surfaces.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Name-In-Marcellus Rule",
        "body": "A proper name (brand, character, nickname, section heading) is Marcellus; any number, button or helper text is Gothic A1.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every counting number (OD, timers, counts) is tabular so columns and live clocks do not jitter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rule-Not-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "To separate or lift something, draw a 1px rule or step the fill. Never add a shadow, blur or glass.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** read every colour from a variable, and verify both `data-faction` themes.",
      "**Do** draw separation with a 1px `--line` rule; use `--line-strong` on interactive borders.",
      "**Do** keep all corners square (0 radius) and badges square.",
      "**Do** keep the orb column identical in every row and the constellation straight and dotted.",
      "**Do** put names in Marcellus and operable text and numbers in Gothic A1 tabular.",
